    "id": "train-6935",
    "question": "An air conditioner running for eight hours would consume 7.2 kilowatts. How many kilowatts would the air conditioner consume if it was used for 6 hours a day for 5 days?",
    "gold": "27",
    "answer": "The air conditioner consumes 7.2/8 = <<7.2/8=0.9>>0.9 kilowatt per hour.\nSo, in 6 hours, it will consume 0.9 kilowatts per hour * 6 hours = <<0.9*6=5.4>>5.4 kilowatts.\nIn 5 days, its total consumption is 5.4 kilowatts * 5 = <<5.4*5=27>>27 kilowatts.\n#### 27"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many kilowatts the air conditioner would consume if it was used for 6 hours a day for 5 days, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the daily consumption of the air conditioner:**\n   - The air conditioner consumes 7.2 kilowatts in 8 hours.\n   - To find the daily consumption, we divide the total consumption by the number of hours it runs in a day:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Daily consumption} = \\frac{7.2 \\text{ kilowatts}}{8 \\text{ hours}} = 0.9 \\text{ kilowatts per hour}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total consumption for 5 days:**\n   - The air conditioner runs for 6 hours each day.\n   - To find the total consumption for 5 days, we multiply the daily consumption by the number of days:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total consumption} = 0.9 \\text{ kilowatts per hour} \\times 6 \\text{ hours per day} \\times 5 \\text{ days} = 27 \\text{ kilowatts}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the air conditioner would consume \\(\\boxed{27}\\) kilowatts if it was used for 6 hours a day for 5 days.",
